+## Compose the title
+
+Use `NN <short role label> · <subject> · <attitude> — <verified project display name>`.
+Take stage/role identity from [the catalogue](../../00-governance/types/agent-catalog.json) and its short label from [Focus choices](focus-choices.md).
+For example: `05 High-Level Architecture · Security · Black — SpeakerCoach`.
+Preserve the established role prefix and project display binding; do not substitute “Architect” or renumber identities from a sample.
+A deliberately unset subject displays `Overall`; an unrecoverable subject displays `Focus unknown`.
+Role None displays `General` without a stage number; unrecoverable role displays `Role unknown` without inventing a prefix.
+Attitude displays the selected canonical English color, Off, or `Attitude unknown`; retain temporary scope in the receipt and reply.
+Goal stays in the receipt, not the title. Unknown project: omit its suffix and report the missing binding.
+Use one line, no secrets or control characters; shorten a long subject faithfully, never the role identity.
+Retain the full subject in the receipt even when its visible label is abbreviated, for example Performance → Perf.
+Retain an explicitly chosen compact subject label for later title recomposition until the subject or label changes; it is presentation metadata, not another focus.
+Honor a directly requested custom title while retaining the computed projection separately; a custom title changes no state.
+
+## Supported native action
+
+Use the current client's supported rename-chat action and its actual schema.
+For `mcp__codex_app__set_thread_title` or `codex_tui.set_thread_title`, pass `title` and omit `threadId` to target this chat.
