+# Independent session fields and readable chat names
+
+This increment adds a thinking attitude and a subject within an existing role. The goal remains in the conversation receipt.
+It implements the 28 October brief using embedded ASDG; OpenSpec and application development remain separate work.
+
+![Goal, role, subject and attitude stay independent in a chat-local receipt; the title displays role, subject and attitude.](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-focus/images/session-fields.svg)
+
+## What changed
+
+- `$asdg-focus 05` still selects High-Level Architecture; `$asdg-focus subject Security` changes only the subject.
+- `$asdg-attitude Black` selects a thinking approach; Green and Off change that approach without losing role, subject or goal.
+- English/Spanish selections, read-only status, explicit temporary scopes and restoration are defined in the [attitude guide](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-attitude/attitudes.md).
+- Titles project the verified role, subject and attitude. Failed renaming preserves valid state and produces a truthful receipt.
+- Focus, Status, Role, Suggestion and team setup share the [session contract](../../../asdg/skills/asdg-focus/session-state.md); templates include the portable discovery adapter.
+
+The unscoped default—retain the attitude until changed or Off—is **proposed for pilot review**, not recorded human acceptance.
+These are agent instructions and conversation receipts; they add no shared session-state file or new persistence service.
+
+## Evidence
+
+| Check | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| Starting point | Clean worktree at `b49a6994a554d3e3a99f6f2bf1d51d53d5246fad`. |
+| Regression suite | 58 tests pass; includes Attitude installation, relocation and repeat-setup preservation. |
+| Project structure | `python3 -B asdg/scripts/cli.py verify` passes. |
+| Package checks | Eight unchanged, pre-existing sibling presentation-link failures; no new package issues. |
+| Generic skill validator | Unavailable because PyYAML is missing; package skill syntax checks ran. |
+| Visual | New editable SVG rendered and inspected at 720 px; embedded Markdown preview not inspected. |
+| Native exercises | Two authorized Architecture chats retained separate subjects; Black → Green → Off, one-answer expiry, read-only status, quoted commands and invalid Purple input behaved as specified. |
+| Titles | Native RENAMED and UNCHANGED observed. Performance's readback was shortened; an explicit Perf. display label produced an exact readback while retaining the full subject. |
+
+Application files, project/lifecycle/sprint state, hook definitions, native role adapters and approval history are protected from this change.
+Modification receipts record changed document hashes; they neither approve the increment nor transfer existing acceptance to new bytes.
+
+## Review and limits
+
+Native resume/compaction, picker refresh, named-review/nested expiry and unavailable/failed rename branches remain unverified; source rules alone do not prove them.
+Tests used the installed skill paths and native chat tools. A shortened readback does not by itself establish storage or visual UI clipping.
+The author also ran these checks; test chats share the same sources and are not an independent review.
+No commit, push, sprint transition, hook-trust change or OpenSpec installation was performed.
+Review the persistence default and the observed title behavior before the next ASDG/OpenSpec increment.
+
